<title>UK: Ryanair considering stock market listing - paper.</title>
<headline>Ryanair considering stock market listing - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Irish low-cost airline Ryanair is considering a stock market flotation which should value it at more than 100 million sterling ($169.5 million), the Sunday Telegraph reported.</p>
<p>The float could be in the U.S., Dublin or London, or &quot;all three, depending on conditions,&quot; the newspaper quoted a source inside the company as saying.</p>
<p>Nobody at Ryanair was available for comment. The airline has declined all comment on such stories in the past.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44-171-542-7717</p>
<p>($1=.5899 Sterling)</p>
